  "tagline": "Real PostgreSQL compiled to WebAssembly: an embeddable Postgres for browsers, Node, Bun and Deno.",
  "description": "PGlite is a WASM build of PostgreSQL packaged as a TypeScript library by ElectricSQL. Rather than emulating Postgres or running a Linux VM, it compiles Postgres' single-user mode to WebAssembly and wraps it with a JS API, so you get genuine Postgres SQL, types and many extensions (pgvector, PostGIS, pg_trgm and more) in about 3 MB gzipped. Data can live in memory, IndexedDB, OPFS or the filesystem, and it integrates with Electric's sync engine for local-first apps. It has become a popular choice for in-browser demos, tests and dev databases, but it is single-connection and not a replacement for a Postgres server.",
